# Bad acquires Lock without a finally Leave (11); Good releases in finally (19) clean
criticalsection-not-released 11
!criticalsection-not-released 19
# TMonitor.Enter/Exit is the SAME contract as Enter/Leave -- Exit in a finally releases.
# GoodMonitor (31): correct Enter/try/finally/Exit idiom -- must be SILENT.
!criticalsection-not-released 31
# NEGATIVE CONTROLS -- these must fire BEFORE and AFTER the fix. Widening the
# release-verb set is exactly the change that can make the rule unable to fire.
# BadMonitorNoExit (43): acquired, never released.
criticalsection-not-released 43
# BadMonitorExitOutsideFinally (51): Exit is present but NOT in a finally.
criticalsection-not-released 51
# BadMonitorMixed: LockA (61) released in finally -> silent; LockB (67) leaked -> fires.
# This pair also proves the key is the LOCK ARGUMENT, not the bare 'tmonitor' receiver.
!criticalsection-not-released 61
criticalsection-not-released 67
